# XCU lp
# Copyright (c) 2026 Nicholas Martin. All rights reserved.
#
# lp is checked only on a path that cannot reach a printer: a file operand
# that does not exist. Submitting a real request would use a device the
# suite must not assume; the printing itself is recorded as untestable.

assertion  XCU.lp.001
anchor     utilities/lp.html#EXIT STATUS
anchor     utilities/lp.html#OPERANDS
class      required
since      1992
says       A file operand that cannot be read gives a non-zero exit status.
test       t/001-missing-file.sh

assertion  XCU.lp.002
anchor     utilities/lp.html#DESCRIPTION
anchor     utilities/lp.html#OPTIONS
anchor     utilities/lp.html#STDOUT
class      untestable
since      1992
says       lp copies its input to a destination device, prints a request ID
           on standard output unless -s is given, and honours -c, -d, -m,
           -n, -o, -t and -w.
reason     Printing needs an output device, which the page leaves
           unspecified and which a test system need not have; the result is
           paper (or another device) outside the reach of a script.
